{
  "name": "settings-det (settings shell + Appearance/Configuration/System/Danger/Update, operator + builder, unsaved-guard, fast-fail on data-dependent)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "Code-verified against routes/Settings.svelte + settings/{Appearance,Configuration,System,Danger,UpdateChecker}.svelte + components/settings/{ConfigFileCard,UnsavedChangesDialog,UnsavedChangesBadge,SettingsToggle}.svelte.",
    "13 nav keys from the CLUSTERS table: appearance, profile, stt, llm, model-hub, configuration, tools, permissions, integrations, system, shortcuts, observability, danger. CLUSTERS are static -> nav is identical in both modes (no uiMode gate).",
    "plan-mode-default-toggle-switch and auto-install-python-deps-toggle-switch are <button role=switch> (Toggle.svelte), NOT <input>. setChecked would throw; we click the -switch instead.",
    "config-file-card-copy-{section} lives inside {#if expanded} in ConfigFileCard.svelte, so the card header (config-file-card-{section}) is clicked first to expand it, then the copy button is asserted and clicked. Sections are a hardcoded vec (runtime/oria/observability, config.rs) and config_path is always set, so both are deterministic.",
    "stt-trigger is a native <select> (Select.svelte) with static options (toggle, push-to-talk); it is exercised via selectOption in the STT save branch alongside the language field, then saved through the unsaved dialog.",
    "UpdateChecker (rendered inside System.svelte) is an external-update boundary: update-checker + update-check-btn are asserted present only and never clicked. update-install-btn renders only when an update is available (data-dependent), so it is NOT asserted.",
    "Danger cards are screenshot-only; no reset btn or confirm dialog is triggered (real resets live in destructive.json).",
    "settings-mobile-nav-toggle / -sheet render only when sidebarState === 'drawer' (mobile); at desktop they are absent, so no waitFor is issued and the desktop state is captured by screenshot only."
  ],
